1
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:10,960
Oh.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
It’s my favorite song.

3
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,320
You two, can you get me some wine?

4
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:24,360
Come on.

5
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:25,320
I’ll grab it.

6
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:27,720
These two are busy being inseparable.

7
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,240
As inseparable as fried dough, really.

8
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:31,800
We are.

9
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,320
Pokpong and I are inseparable.

10
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,480
We come as a set.

11
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:36,880
Sure.

12
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,800
He’s right.

13
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:40,880
Come on.

14
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,080
Let’s celebrate.

15
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:42,480
Come here.

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,360
Hurry up.

17
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:45,880
Is this enough?

18
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:46,680
Okay.

19
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:47,680
Oh, I thought that was for me.

20
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:50,080
Here it is.

21
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:50,960
Here.

22
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:51,600
Hey!

23
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,000
You know I’m waiting.

24
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:53,440
I’m waiting.

25
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:54,280
Thank you.

26
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,520
Uncle Tul, don’t tease Mom like that.

27
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:56,960
This one must be mine.

28
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:58,240
Give it to me.

29
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,640
Okay.

30
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:07,080
Let’s celebrate the special 200-piece order.

31
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,600
Let’s celebrate finally quitting a job.

32
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:15,440
Let’s celebrate the most chic art glass studio

33
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:18,440
for having the most beautiful mom
as the manager.

34
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:19,960
That’s not all.

35
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:23,680
Let’s celebrate both of your futures.

36
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,840
Love Mini for a long time.

37
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:27,440
Of course.

38
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,880
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

39
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,440
I’m sure good at opening wine.

40
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,160
Ta-da!

41
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:38,800
It looks amazing.

42
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:40,560
Should we just eat the cake first?

43
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,320
No way.

44
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:41,880
Let’s have dinner first.

45
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,000
You guys are too sweet.

46
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:44,920
What did you eat, Uncle Tul?

47
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,320
Okay.

48
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,680
Don’t you think they’re always so sweet?

49
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:48,440
I do.

50
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:49,680
You probably don’t need

51
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,440
I’ll give it a try, Mom.

52
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:05,840
Your cake is the best.

53
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:07,400
I’m confident.

54
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,280
Do you really like it?

55
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:10,440
I really do.

56
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,080
You wanna try it?

57
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:11,640
No, thanks.

58
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,360
I’ve had some.

59
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:13,960
You should eat, Mini.

60
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,080
What?

61
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:17,440
I told you I had some, Mom.

62
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,720
Pokpong, you should eat and eat lots.

63
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:20,880
Have a bite.

64
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:21,360
Eat more.

65
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:22,960
I have to go.

66
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:24,440
What?

67
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,800
Wait, wait. Why?

68
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,360
Why don’t you stay and
celebrate with your nephew?

69
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,080
Hmm…

70
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,560
Where are you going?

71
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,440
You’re not staying over?

72
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:43,280
I have a date.

73
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,240
What?

74
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,400
I have a date.

75
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,480
For the first time in 300 years, it seems.

76
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:51,720
Just let me go.

77
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,600
Well, then, go all the way.

78
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:55,760
You pervert!

79
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,600
Bye.

80
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,480
And you, tone it down!

81
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,440
Goodbye, Uncle.

82
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,000
Bye.

83
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:11,840
Here.

84
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:18,680
Have one more.

85
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:09,400
Is it the rain?

86
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,120
I think so.

87
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,560
Pokpong!

88
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:30,480
Pokpong!

89
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,080
Come here!

90
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,040
Come!

91
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,040
Come here!

92
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:36,560
Let go!

93
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:40,400
Let go!

94
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:42,520
Pokpong!

95
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,400
No!

96
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,560
Mom!

97
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,840
Mom!

98
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:54,960
Mom!

99
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:57,160
Mom!

100
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,840
Shut up!

101
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:02,360
Mini.

102
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,120
Mini…

103
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,720
(TWO YEARS LATER)

104
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:41,240
What the hell?

105
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,360
Mao?

106
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,520
Mao, is that you?

107
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,120
Mao?

108
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,200
Don’t play with me!

109
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,520
Mao?

110
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,560
“Pain molded me.”

111
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,560
“Patience gave me shape.”

112
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:19,280
“Every wound is a crack
that hasn’t broken.”

113
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:31,160
“And I chose to reshape it.”

114
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,520
How can I help?

115
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,360
I’m here to see Mr. Mini.

116
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,920
You’d usually need
an appointment for that.

117
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,440
I don’t have much time.

118
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:09,320
Okay.

119
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:17,960
Coffee?

120
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:19,600
Who was that man just now?

121
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:22,600
Uncle Tul.

122
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:23,640
My mom’s younger brother.

123
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,480
He’s the manager here.

124
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,000
How long does he live here?

125
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,720
Coffee?

126
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,800
How many years has he been working here?

127
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:39,640
Sure.

128
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:40,760
Coffee, it is.

129
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,360
He started working here
since Mom was gone.

130
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,120
Hmm…

131
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:52,880
How many people live here?

132
00:11:58,920 --> 00:11:59,800
I live here alone.

133
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,040
Oh, what about your uncle?

134
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,240
He commutes.

135
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:07,960
Okay.

136
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,600
I don’t know who you live with or
who you’re related to, you know?

137
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,240
Let’s cut to the chase, then.

138
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:24,280
On Friday, February 13,
between 7 p.m. to midnight,

139
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,840
where were you?

140
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:27,560
Why?

141
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,200
Just tell me where you were.

142
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:32,920
I was out drinking.

143
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,320
Who were you with?

144
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,240
Do you have an alibi?

145
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:49,720
I went alone.

146
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,200
You can ask anyone at the bar.

147
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:56,960
Give me names, please.

148
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,160
Hey.

149
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:01,400
Do you usually ask for
everybody’s name at the bar?

150
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,600
Then please tell me the name of the bar.

151
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,520
I’ll ask around.

152
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:09,360
The police at the precinct already
asked me these questions.

153
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,720
You didn’t talk to them?

154
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,520
If there are no more new questions, excuse me.

155
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:16,640
I have work.

156
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,400
I don’t want to play a staring game.

157
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:19,320
Hey.

158
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:24,000
Do you realize you’re one of the suspects
for the Horse’s murder?

159
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:33,680
My name is Kongphon.

160
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,480
I asked to be assigned to this case

161
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:39,880
because I thought this might have something to do with your case

162
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:40,680
from two years ago.

163
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:44,720
I don’t care whose questions you answered before.

164
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,720
Just answer mine.

165
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,120
You smell suspicious.

166
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,840
And you…

167
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,560
You reek of alcohol.

168
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,360
Do you usually use your mouth?

169
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:23,920
Excuse me?

170
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:28,680
If you don’t use your mouth to work,
it means you can work and talk.

171
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,720
You said you have work, right?

172
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,120
Let’s go to work.

173
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,640
You work.

174
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:34,760
I ask.

175
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,720
You answer.

176
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,280
We’re not wasting anyone’s time.

177
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:40,080
First question first.

178
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,200
What does the name of your studio mean?

179
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:45,520
It means…

180
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:48,520
It means…

181
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,720
“My business.”

182
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,800
Okay.

183
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,000
It’s also “my business” now.

184
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:01,360
Come on.

185
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:11,200
Where is it?

186
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,080
Where is it?

187
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:30,560
Where’s your office?

188
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,560
You have 10 minutes.

189
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:52,680
10 minutes.

190
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,040
New questions only.

191
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:54,640
Start.

192
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:57,840
Do you eat anything all day?

193
00:15:58,840 --> 00:15:59,280
What?

194
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:01,520
How’s that for new questions?

195
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:03,680
No one asked you that before, huh?

196
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:06,880
If you’re just going to pull my leg,

197
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,000
just go home.

198
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:09,240
I have so many things to do.

199
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:10,600
Okay, okay, okay.

200
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:11,400
I’m gonna be serious.

201
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:14,280
Let me ask you this…

202
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,000
The blurb on your poster.

203
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:18,520
It says…

204
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,960
“Pain molded me.”

205
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:24,800
“Patience gave me shape.”

206
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:28,480
“Every wound is a crack
that hasn’t broken.”

207
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:30,000
What does it mean?

208
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,280
It’s the concept of my work.

209
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:34,440
Recycled glass art.

210
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:37,320
Broken glasses could be reshaped.

211
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:40,080
We just use some pretty words to sell it.

212
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:40,880
That’s it.

213
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,160
Next question.

214
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:43,600
Hmm…

215
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,160
A fire like that…

216
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,640
A man would burn to a crisp
in there, wouldn’t it?

217
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,080
Wouldn’t you want to know?

218
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:56,880
Hey.

219
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:57,880
Mr. Mini.

220
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:01,040
Can you take a look at these photos?

221
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,480
These are from the crime scene.

222
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,520
The police withheld these from the press

223
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,480
to keep the investigation unaffected.

224
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,680
Anything familiar to you?

225
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:30,240
The horse mask that the victim was wearing
while being brutally murdered…

226
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:36,080
It might share something
with the masked men that attacked you two years ago.

227
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,280
And?

228
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:44,120
So I’m wondering if there’s a connection.

229
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:47,560
Do you know anything about this?

230
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,160
Mini.

231
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,120
You have a parcel delivery.

232
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,320
They need you to inspect it before accepting it.

233
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:57,360
Yes, Uncle.

234
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:58,360
I’ll be there.

235
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,320
I don’t know anything about this,

236
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,600
and I’ll tell you one thing.

237
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,760
Those masked men
are not just familiar to me,

238
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:11,080
but they are unforgettable.

239
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:15,360
I don’t like you questioning me
as if I’m a suspect.

240
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,680
Will you please calm down?

241
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,960
I was wronged.

242
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,560
I was the victim

243
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,840
whom the police didn’t freaking help.

244
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,880
If you’re going to be here again,

245
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,120
give me a heads up so I can call my lawyer.

246
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,120
I don’t want to be a scapegoat.

247
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:33,800
Okay.

248
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:37,080
You can have a lawyer with you next time.

249
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,360
I just want to help you.

250
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:42,080
Excuse me.

251
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:45,280
Good day, sir.

252
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,160
Parcel delivery, my ass.

253
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:27,960
Nice, isn’t it?

254
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,560
It’s nice to see a hardworking cop
like him for once.

255
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,680
It’s been almost two years,

256
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,920
and they’re asking questions now?

257
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:49,080
The suspect holds a grudge,

258
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,480
and is emotionally unstable.

259
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:55,680
He is sad and seems to have trust issues.

260
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,720
His reaction when he saw the mask…

261
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,800
He was stunned and surprised.

262
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:06,840
The other guy…

263
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,400
Very interesting.

264
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:13,720
Given their relationship, he has enough motive.

265
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,000
Reminder:

266
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:26,040
The suspect is too small to do this alone.

267
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:41,920
Just make sure this doesn’t affect our project.

268
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,280
Okay?

269
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,680
Uh, excuse me.

270
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:25,760
Yes?

271
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:32,040
I have some homework on political satire.

272
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,520
Can you recommend a book?

273
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:35,400
Of course.

274
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,800
I’ll recommend a famous one.

275
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,560
I’m sure your professor will love it.

276
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:46,960
Here it is.

277
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,680
It is the story of farm animals that
rebel against their human master.

278
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:52,720
Social equality.

279
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,080
I think it’s a good idea.

280
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:56,960
Oh, and…

281
00:21:58,120 --> 00:21:59,920
Can I have your contact?

282
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,640
Just in case I need something else.

283
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,240
I’m sure this one book will do.

284
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:34,680
Nut.

285
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:43,840
How many times have I told you

286
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:45,960
not to meet me here?

287
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,160
Jan is missing.

288
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:52,920
I can’t contact her.

289
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:58,320
And how many times have I told you

290
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,480
not to show up here when
I’m on my lunch break?

291
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:04,960
It’s my personal time.

292
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:08,480
Are you insane?

293
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:11,560
Didn’t you hear me tell you Jan is missing?

294
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:16,960
You can still eat?

295
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,560
Jan is missing.

296
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,880
You should be worried about that more than anyone.

297
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:32,320
Can you get it together?

298
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:44,800
How are you still so calm?

299
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,520
Everyone’s panicking.

300
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,560
My brother is dead.

301
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:04,080
My little brother is freaking dead!

302
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,520
His corpse was wearing the horse mask.

303
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:15,800
You know damn well what that means.

304
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,760
One is dead. One is missing.

305
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:24,440
Don’t you think something is strange?

306
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,240
The police are working on your brother’s case.

307
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:30,760
It’s gonna take some time

308
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,000
since your brother had many enemies.

309
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:34,880
You know that.

310
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,360
As for Jan…

311
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:43,280
She probably just went somewhere.

312
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,400
Didn’t she say her grandmother lives alone?

313
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:50,120
Did you look at her grandmother’s house?

314
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:52,160
But why doesn’t she answer the phone?

315
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:54,120
She doesn’t post anything, either.

316
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:55,240
That just doesn’t sound like her.

317
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:58,360
How’d I know that?

318
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:03,040
She’ll be back soon.

319
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:05,560
I’ll say it one more time…

320
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,920
Don’t come meet me here again.

321
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,560
She’s really loyal to you.

322
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:26,480
Don’t act like she doesn’t matter.

323
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:55,040
MAO

324
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:14,760
- Koh.
- (Why didn’t you answer your phone?)

325
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:15,760
Claim Approval speaking.

326
00:26:16,440 --> 00:26:17,400
He doesn’t give a damn.

327
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,000
(He even told me to go.)

328
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:20,840
Should we meet up tonight?

329
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:22,800
I’m stressed out.

330
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,120
Yes. Of course.

331
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:28,240
The details are the same.

332
00:26:29,760 --> 00:26:30,120
Yes.

333
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:30,920
Goodbye.

334
00:26:33,120 --> 00:26:33,440
Yes?

335
00:26:33,720 --> 00:26:36,520
Some clients have been contactingus about their documents.

336
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:39,320
These are Ms. Jan’s cases,from Customer Service.

337
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:41,960
I’m not sure if Ms. Jan is on vacation,

338
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:43,480
but I can’t contact her at all.

339
00:26:45,760 --> 00:26:47,920
I’m not sure about that as well.

340
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:52,520
But just transfer the cases to me
since the clients are waiting.

341
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:53,680
Roger.

342
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:54,600
Alright.

343
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:55,520
Thank you.

344
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:12,480
(There were five of them…)

345
00:27:14,560 --> 00:27:15,440
(One of them was a woman.)

346
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:21,120
(Besides their voices, heights,
and estimated ages,)

347
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:23,520
(do you remember anything else?)

348
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:25,680
(They…)

349
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:29,720
(They spilled a name.)

350
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,080
(What is the name?)

351
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:36,840
Koh, watch out!

352
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:38,520
Koh.

353
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:40,080
Koh.

354
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:44,920
(He’s older than her.)

355
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:50,440
(Which mask was this man called Koh wearing?)

356
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:02,920
Sheep.

357
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:10,480
The woman was wearing a dog mask.

358
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:17,720
There were… a horse, a monkey…

359
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:25,080
and a rabbit.

360
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:28,520
I don’t know who they are.

361
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:34,040
(I want you to think carefully)

362
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:41,120
(whether you and your family
have had any conflict with anyone.)

363
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:45,800
(Maybe it was an unintentional conflict)

364
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:48,640
(that leads to unexpected consequences.)

365
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:57,800
Pokpong

366
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:00,720
was the nicest man

367
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:04,480
I’ve ever met in my life.

368
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:38,760
Boss!

369
00:29:41,160 --> 00:29:41,760
You hungry?

370
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,880
I got you some noodles.

371
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:01,440
You want some dessert?

372
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:07,920
Is this your first meal?

373
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:09,440
You were out all day, after all.

374
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:11,080
Yeah.

375
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:14,200
I went to see the glassblower today.

376
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:18,080
Honestly,

377
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:22,200
what were you thinking
digging up Mr. Mini’s case?

378
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:23,520
You wanna know?

379
00:30:29,240 --> 00:30:29,880
(Rabbit…)

380
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:35,120
(ordered Horse…)

381
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:46,520
(to be the first to rape me.)

382
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:51,120
Methas’ hands were tied behind his back.

383
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:53,200
His pants piled on his thighs.

384
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:54,840
He was naked from the waist down.

385
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:56,480
Now listen to this.

386
00:30:59,200 --> 00:30:59,880
(So…)

387
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:04,280
(You weren’t raped by one person?)

388
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:13,000
(Yes.)

389
00:31:17,520 --> 00:31:18,440
(The other rapist was Sheep.)

390
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:25,040
That day, Mini, or Mr. Manus, was found
with his pants piling on his thighs,

391
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:28,320
face down, hands tied.

392
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:29,960
What do you think?

393
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:33,320
Are you…

394
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:35,760
Are you suggesting that

395
00:31:37,440 --> 00:31:38,960
Mr. Mini killed Horse?

396
00:31:43,760 --> 00:31:44,840
He’s too small.

397
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,920
I don’t think he can do it alone.

398
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:52,960
The size of the shoes
we found at the crime scene is 45.

399
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,600
Mini’s is 39.

400
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:58,080
How’d you know that?

401
00:31:58,560 --> 00:31:59,280
Did you ask him that?

402
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:01,160
Yours is 43.

403
00:32:05,040 --> 00:32:05,840
Holy crap!

404
00:32:07,280 --> 00:32:08,480
You’re so cool!

405
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:10,840
That’s my boss.

406
00:32:11,320 --> 00:32:11,960
Well, Sin.

407
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:16,920
Look up places that make masks
like those customizable ones.

408
00:32:17,360 --> 00:32:21,240
Check back their orders to the last 4-6 months.

409
00:32:22,480 --> 00:32:23,040
Yes, boss.

410
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:25,800
Where you going?

411
00:32:26,120 --> 00:32:26,600
I need a drink.

412
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:28,840
Throw the trash on my desk away for me.

413
00:33:07,840 --> 00:33:08,480
Oh.

414
00:33:09,440 --> 00:33:10,480
A new customer.

415
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:13,160
I’ve never seen you around here before.

416
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:14,760
Hello, handsome.

417
00:33:15,320 --> 00:33:15,960
What would you like?

418
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:19,160
First drink’s on me, what do you say?

419
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:20,640
Okay.

420
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:24,840
If it’s on you, then I’ll drink anything.

421
00:33:38,360 --> 00:33:38,840
Thank you.

422
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:57,840
Oh, hey.

423
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:00,640
I’m looking for someone.

424
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:02,000
He’s about…

425
00:34:03,160 --> 00:34:03,760
this height.

426
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:05,400
His eyes are big.

427
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:08,560
He has a stubborn face.

428
00:34:09,240 --> 00:34:10,760
Like… damn stubborn.

429
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:21,160
Stubborn like a daredevil, like he’s ready for a fight?

430
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:23,440
But…

431
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:28,920
Damn cute, though.

432
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:30,960
Who is cute?

433
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:52,040
Mao.

434
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:57,000
So you’re going to see if
Jan went to her grandmother's?

435
00:35:01,320 --> 00:35:02,320
I don’t even know where that is.

436
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:04,840
Jan only said it’s in Lopburi.

437
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:13,520
Honestly, I’m not okay that we can’t reach her.

438
00:35:15,640 --> 00:35:17,720
For her not to post any Stories,
it’s just unlikely.

439
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:23,320
Maybe you’re so stressed out
about Mhok that you’re losing it.

440
00:35:24,240 --> 00:35:24,720
Come on.

441
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:28,560
The way Mhok died was pretty spooky.

442
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:32,400
You know exactly what it meant.

443
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:34,160
It wasn’t normal.

444
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:37,920
Mao.

445
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:39,600
Think about it.

446
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:44,320
No one ever knows what we did these past two years.

447
00:35:46,800 --> 00:35:49,040
There were no cameras in that damn house.

448
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:51,200
Even the police couldn't find us.

449
00:35:52,120 --> 00:35:53,480
No one saw what we looked like.

450
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:56,760
How could it have anything to do
with Mhok’s death?

451
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:08,520
Honestly…

452
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:15,040
Did Mhok ever use that damn mask
to do something stupid after that?

453
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:23,160
Nut said to burn them down.

454
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:26,400
Did you?

455
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:29,560
I did.

456
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:31,840
But Mhok…

457
00:36:35,080 --> 00:36:36,560
I think he wore it once or twice.

458
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:38,200
But that was it.

459
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:41,680
I think he might have burned it already.

460
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,640
I couldn’t find it anywhere in the house.

461
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:46,280
Damn it.

462
00:36:47,240 --> 00:36:48,000
And…

463
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:51,560
Where did he wear it to?

464
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:57,600
He wore it to his friend’s Halloween party.

465
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:00,480
Come on.

466
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:02,720
It was just for a friend’s house party.

467
00:37:03,040 --> 00:37:04,000
It’s not like he wore it outside.

468
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:10,520
He told me he got into some trouble that day,

469
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:12,520
but it was about some woman.

470
00:37:13,640 --> 00:37:13,880
What?

471
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:15,000
Hey.

472
00:37:16,480 --> 00:37:18,000
If my brother died because of his stupid ass,

473
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:20,200
I’d get it.

474
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:21,400
I know him well.

475
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,040
But I don’t get that position.

476
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:25,800
Who’d have thought it would be like that?

477
00:37:26,920 --> 00:37:27,760
You don’t think it’s strange, really?

478
00:37:36,240 --> 00:37:36,760
How about this?

479
00:37:38,120 --> 00:37:42,240
I’ll check Jan’s profile to see who her emergency contact is.

480
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:44,040
You deal with the rest.

481
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:45,320
Okay?

482
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:47,880
Shit.

483
00:37:49,320 --> 00:37:52,520
If it goes on any longer than this,
we’re all going to be in trouble.

484
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:56,800
Everything we’ve been doing,
if anyone takes over us, we’re doomed.

485
00:37:57,840 --> 00:38:00,040
Good thing I managed to find someone
to replace your brother.

486
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:01,440
That’s exactly why.

487
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:03,680
Nut is so ignorant of all this that he pisses me off.

488
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:06,800
He’s not worried because he’s on
his pedestal ordering us around.

489
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:08,600
It’s us who’s gonna be in trouble.

490
00:38:09,160 --> 00:38:09,680
Come on.

491
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:13,160
You just deal with Jan’s matter.

492
00:38:14,120 --> 00:38:14,960
I’ll talk to Nut.

493
00:38:25,680 --> 00:38:27,080
This place has some amazing plum wine.

494
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:29,200
It’s homemade.

495
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:32,040
When did you come in?

496
00:38:33,440 --> 00:38:35,400
My eyes were glued to the door.

497
00:38:38,200 --> 00:38:39,640
There’s a backdoor here.

498
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:41,560
You ever used it?

499
00:38:46,680 --> 00:38:52,080
So when you enter, people might not
know when exactly that is?

500
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:53,440
Am I right?

501
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:56,720
Mr. Kongphon.

502
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,200
You’re off work.

503
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:01,120
Can you stop working for a sec?

504
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:07,280
Wow!

505
00:39:08,560 --> 00:39:10,520
I was just wondering who you’re here with.

506
00:39:12,440 --> 00:39:13,200
It’s nothing.

507
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,160
This man here is a cop.

508
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:19,600
He’s suspecting that I… killed someone.

509
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:20,520
Oh, damn.

510
00:39:21,520 --> 00:39:23,760
I should have made you drink
some dog-infused liquor, then!

511
00:39:24,160 --> 00:39:24,840
Oh, come on.

512
00:39:25,240 --> 00:39:25,720
Why?

513
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:26,600
Why not?

514
00:39:27,240 --> 00:39:28,560
Is there such a thing as
a dog-infused liquor?

515
00:39:28,680 --> 00:39:29,240
Yeah.

516
00:39:30,560 --> 00:39:31,200
You want some?

517
00:39:45,440 --> 00:39:46,640
Let’s play shot roulette.

518
00:39:48,080 --> 00:39:51,920
Whoever the shot glass points to,
he answers a question.

519
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:55,520
If he doesn’t answer, he takes a shot.

520
00:39:56,200 --> 00:39:56,920
Who pays?

521
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,080
We’ll take turns.

522
00:39:58,680 --> 00:40:00,400
The one with more secrets pays more.

523
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:01,520
Okay.

524
00:40:02,240 --> 00:40:03,080
Fair enough.

525
00:40:08,520 --> 00:40:09,000
Ready?

526
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:20,520
Fire away.

527
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:24,600
What makes you think I’m a murderer?

528
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:27,080
I’m not sure yet.

529
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:42,040
Why aren’t you sure?

530
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:44,400
I don’t have any evidence.

531
00:40:59,240 --> 00:41:00,040
Alright. Fire away.

532
00:41:01,120 --> 00:41:02,000
Do you have a boyfriend?

533
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:03,840
Hold on.

534
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:05,960
Where did that come from?

535
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:18,840
Are you still in love with your boyfriend?

536
00:41:40,640 --> 00:41:42,080
He was the only person in the world

537
00:41:44,280 --> 00:41:45,400
who understood me.

538
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:49,680
Met everyone in the world, have you?

539
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:56,360
You didn’t answer my question.

540
00:41:56,680 --> 00:41:57,400
What’s the question?

541
00:41:57,720 --> 00:41:58,560
Do I have a boyfriend?

542
00:41:59,280 --> 00:41:59,800
No.

543
00:42:00,520 --> 00:42:03,880
And I don’t think there’s anyone
in the world who would get me.

544
00:42:05,720 --> 00:42:07,600
Have you tried?

545
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:17,080
Everyone is hard to understand.

546
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:23,440
That’s why people who understand us mean so much.

547
00:42:38,920 --> 00:42:41,880
If you had a chance to take revenge
on the people who hurt you,

548
00:42:42,240 --> 00:42:42,800
would you take it?

549
00:42:53,480 --> 00:42:53,960
In a heartbeat.

550
00:43:00,640 --> 00:43:02,120
Sometimes what happens in one’s past

551
00:43:03,880 --> 00:43:05,240
makes one forget

552
00:43:07,280 --> 00:43:09,760
who one really is

553
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:11,960
and what one is capable of.

554
00:43:19,440 --> 00:43:19,840
Oh.

555
00:43:20,440 --> 00:43:21,280
My favorite song.

556
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:25,600
It’s been so long since I last saw him.

557
00:44:25,960 --> 00:44:27,840
He was gone for almost half a year.

558
00:44:28,920 --> 00:44:30,400
No one could contact him.

559
00:44:30,480 --> 00:44:31,840
I honestly thought he was dead.

560
00:44:32,400 --> 00:44:35,280
And when I asked him, he just said
he needed some time to lick his wound.

561
00:44:35,640 --> 00:44:36,320
Wound, he said.

562
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:39,520
With how lively he looks,

563
00:44:39,960 --> 00:44:41,480
he’s pretty intense when drunk.

564
00:44:41,960 --> 00:44:44,520
I saw him weeping once.

565
00:44:46,920 --> 00:44:48,640
If I went through what Mini did,

566
00:44:49,400 --> 00:44:50,920
I might have already gone insane.

567
00:45:19,280 --> 00:45:20,160
Where did you sleep last night?

568
00:45:21,280 --> 00:45:21,960
A cop’s house.

569
00:45:22,200 --> 00:45:22,480
What?

570
00:45:23,240 --> 00:45:24,040
Was that intentional?

571
00:45:24,480 --> 00:45:25,120
What were you thinking?

572
00:45:27,240 --> 00:45:28,240
It’s best you stay away from him.

573
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:30,000
I want to talk to you.

574
00:45:32,680 --> 00:45:33,760
Where did you go, Jan?

575
00:45:35,320 --> 00:45:36,400
Burning Vengeance.

576
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:39,280
Now I’m getting interested.

577
00:45:40,920 --> 00:45:42,680
I don’t want to eat anymore.

578
00:45:45,240 --> 00:45:45,720
Hey.

579
00:45:47,320 --> 00:45:49,000
Did you miss me so much you couldn’t take it?

580
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:51,240
I need to talk to you about something.

581
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:54,320
Why don’t we get to know each other?

582
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:55,320
Hey!

583
00:45:55,480 --> 00:45:56,200
You don’t like it?
